RL for the image. Let me analyze it to find the current dates of filing for green card categories:', action=<ActionType.MCP: 'call_tool_mcp'>, security_risk=None), MCPObservation(content='{\"meta\": null, \"content\": [{\"type\": \"text\", \"text\": \"The image provided is a table that outlines the current dates for filing green card applications under various categories and for different countries of origin. Here\\'s a detailed breakdown of the information:\\\\n\\\\n---\\\\n\\\\n### **Table Overview:**\\\\n\\\\nThe table is divided into several columns, each representing a specific category or country of origin. The rows correspond to different priority levels or sets of visas.\\\\n\\\\n#### **Columns:**\\\\n1. **Employment-Based**: This column lists the general employment-based visa categories.\\\\n2. **All Chargeability Areas Except Those Listed**: This column provides the filing dates for applicants from all countries except those specifically listed in the subsequent columns.\\\\n3. **CHINA - mainland born**: This column provides the filing dates for applicants who are mainland-born Chinese citizens.\\\\n4. **INDIA**: This column provides the filing dates for Indian applicants.\\\\n5. **MEXICO**: This column provides the filing dates for Mexican applicants.\\\\n6. **PHILIPPINES**: This column provides the filing dates for Filipino applicants.\\\\n\\\\n#### **Rows:**\\\\n\\\\n1. **1st Priority (EB-1)**:\\\\n   - **All Chargeability Areas Except Those Listed**: C (Current)\\\\n   - **CHINA - mainland born**: 01JAN23\\\\n   - **INDIA**: 15APR22\\\\n   - **MEXICO**: C (Current)\\\\n   - **PHILIPPINES**: C (Current)\\\\n\\\\n   **Interpretation**: For EB-1 visas, applicants from all countries except China, India, Mexico, and the Philippines can file immediately (C). Chinese applicants can file starting January 1, 2023. Indian applicants can file starting April 15, 2022. Mexican and Filipino applicants can also file immediately.\\\\n\\\\n2. **2nd Priority (EB-2)**:\\\\n   - **All Chargeability Areas Except Those Listed**: 01AUG23\\\\n   - **CHINA - mainland born**: 01OCT20\\\\n   - **INDIA**: 01JAN13\\\\n   - **MEXICO**: 01AUG23\\\\n   - **PHILIPPINES**: 01AUG23\\\\n\\\\n   **Interpretation**: For EB-2 visas, applicants from all countries except China, India, Mexico, and the Philippines can file starting August 1, 2023. Chinese applicants can file starting October 1, 2020. Indian applicants can file starting January 13, 2013. Mexican and Filipino applicants can file starting August 1, 2023.\\\\n\\\\n3. **3rd Priority (EB-3)**:\\\\n   - **All Chargeability Areas Except Those Listed**: 01MAR23\\\\n   - **CHINA - mainland born**: 15NOV20\\\\n   - **INDIA**: 08JUN13\\\\n   - **MEXICO**: 01MAR23\\\\n   - **PHILIPPINES**: 01MAR23\\\\n\\\\n   **Interpretation**: For EB-3 visas, applicants from all countries except China, India, Mexico, and the Philippines can file starting March 1, 2023. Chinese applicants can file starting November 15, 2020. Indian applicants can file starting June 8, 2013. Mexican and Filipino applicants can file starting March 1, 2023.\\\\n\\\\n4. **Other Workers (EB-3)**:\\\\n   - **All Chargeability Areas Except Those Listed**: 01FEB21\\\\n   - **CHINA - mainland born**: 01FEB21\\\\n   - **INDIA**: 01FEB21\\\\n   - **MEXICO**: 01FEB21\\\\n   - **PHILIPPINES**: 01FEB21\\\\n\\\\n   **Interpretation**: For the \\\\\"Other Workers\\\\\" subcategory of EB-3 visas, applicants from all countries, including China, India, Mexico, and the Philippines, can file starting February 1, 2021.\\\\n\\\\n5. **4th Priority (EB-4)**:\\\\n   - **All Chargeability Areas Except Those Listed**: 01FEB21\\\\n   - **CHINA - mainland born**: 01FEB21\\\\n   - **INDIA**: 01FEB21\\\\n   - **MEXICO**: 01FEB21\\\\n   - **PHILIPPINES**: 01FEB21\\\\n\\\\n   **Interpretation**: For EB-4 visas, applicants from all countries, including China, India, Mexico, and the Philippines, can file starting February 1, 2021.\\\\n\\\\n6. **5th Set Aside (Rural - 20%)**:\\\\n   - **All Chargeability Areas Except Those Listed**: C (Current)\\\\n   - **CHINA - mainland born**: C (Current)\\\\n   - **INDIA**: C (Current)\\\\n   - **MEXICO**: C (Current)\\\\n   - **PHILIPPINES**: C (Current)\\\\n\\\\n   **Interpretation**: For the 5th set-aside visa category (Rural - 20%), applicants from all countries, including China, India, Mexico, and the Philippines, can file immediately (C).\\\\n\\\\n7. **5th Set Aside (High Unemployment - 10%)**:\\\\n   - **All Chargeability Areas Except Those Listed**: C (Current)\\\\n   - **CHINA - mainland born**: C (Current)\\\\n   - **INDIA**: C (Current)\\\\n   - **MEXICO**: C (Current)\\\\n   - **PHILIPPINES**: C (Current)\\\\n\\\\n   **Interpretation**: For the 5th set-aside visa category (High Unemployment - 10%), applicants from all countries, including China, India, Mexico, and the Philippines, can file immediately (C).\\\\n\\\\n8. **5th Set Aside (Infrastructure - 2%)**:\\\\n   - **All Chargeability Areas Except Those Listed**: C (Current)\\\\n   - **CHINA - mainland born**: C (Current)\\\\n   - **INDIA**: C (Current)\\\\n   - **MEXICO**: C (Current)\\\\n   - **PHILIPPINES**: C (Current)\\\\n\\\\n   **Interpretation**: For the 5th set-aside visa category (Infrastructure - 2%), applicants from all countries, including China, India, Mexico, and the Philippines, can file immediately (C).\\\\n\\\\n---\\\\n\\\\n### **Summary of Current Filing Dates:**\\\\n\\\\n- **EB-1**: \\\\n  - All countries except China, India, Mexico, and the Philippines: C (Current)\\\\n  - China: 01JAN23\\\\n  - India: 15APR22\\\\n  - Mexico: C (Current)\\\\n  - Philippines: C (Current)\\\\n\\\\n- **EB-2**: \\\\n  - All countries except China, India, Mexico, and the Philippines: 01AUG23\\\\n  - China: 01OCT20\\\\n  - India: 01JAN13\\\\n  - Mexico: 01AUG23\\\\n  - Philippines: 01AUG23\\\\n\\\\n- **EB-3**: \\\\n  - All countries except China, India, Mexico, and the Philippines: 01MAR23\\\\n  - China: 15NOV20\\\\n  - India: 08JUN13\\\\n  - Mexico: 01MAR23\\\\n  - Philippines: 01MAR23\\\\n\\\\n- **Other Workers (EB-3)**: 01FEB21 (all countries)\\\\n\\\\n- **EB-4**: 01FEB21 (all countries)\\\\n\\\\n- **5th Set Aside (Rural - 20%)**: C (Current) (all countries)\\\\n\\\\n- **5th Set Aside (High Unemployment - 10%)**: C (Current) (all countries)\\\\n\\\\n- **5th Set Aside (Infrastructure - 2%)**: C (Current) (all countries)\\\\n\\\\n---\\\\n\\\\n### **Conclusion:**\\\\n\\\\nThe current filing dates for green card applications vary depending on the visa category and the applicant\\'s country of origin. Applicants should check the specific date for their category and country to determine when they can file. For most categories, applicants from countries other than China, India, Mexico, and the Philippines have more recent filing dates compared to those from these four countries. The 5th set-aside categories (Rural, High Unemployment, and Infrastructure) are currently open for filing for all countries.\", \"annotations\": null}], \"isError\": false}', observation=<ObservationType.MCP: 'mcp'>, name='analyze_image_with_qwen', arguments={'prompt': 'What are the current dates of filing for green card applications shown in this image? Please read all the text in the image carefully, including the categories and their corresponding filing dates.', 'image_url': 'https://files.catbox.moe/rg5fo0.png'}), MCPAction(name='get_platform_guide_list', arguments={'platform': 'RocketChat'}, thought=\"Now I have successfully analyzed the image and extracted all the green card filing dates. However, I need to know Priya Sharma's specific category to provide her with the correct filing date. Since she's a technical writer, I should ask her about her specific employment-based category and country of birth. Let me check if there are any SOPs for RocketChat to communicate with her:\", action=<ActionType.MCP: 'call_tool_mcp'>, security_risk=None), MCPObservation(content='{\"meta\": null, \"content\": [{\"type\": \"text\",